## Hard bans (run `scripts/bans.sh`)

Raw hex or oklch outside the token file; raw palette classes for
semantic states; pure black/white; urgency animation classes;
layout-property transitions; side-stripe accents; gradient text;
`lorem` / `Acme` / `John Doe`. Your generator-managed component
library ({e.g. `src/components/ui/`}) is exempt: it is token-driven.

## Behavioral floor

Visible state (landmarks stay put), disabled-not-hidden, object then
action, discoverable then fast, verbs on buttons, undo over
confirmation, modes visible and escapable, honest feedback in the
user's words, trustworthy representation, keyboard and assistive
parity. A change proposed against any of these runs the verdict
protocol first: protected functions, counted evidence, behavior, then
better / different / costume.
